<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the generated Info.plist by the Tauri CLI, which looks for this
  file by name next to tauri.conf.json. No config key points at it.

  Why it has to exist: macOS hands no capture device to a process whose bundle
  does not say what it wants one for. TCC does not refuse loudly — the webview
  simply enumerates zero devices, and the page reports "device not found"
  rather than "permission denied". That is the whole difference between a user
  who declined a prompt and a prompt that was never allowed to appear.

  This covers the OS layer only. The WKWebView layer is already permissive:
  wry 0.57 implements requestMediaCapturePermissionForOrigin and, with no
  handler registered, answers WKPermissionDecision::Grant. See the report in
  src-tauri/src/pane_webview.rs.

  `tauri dev` builds no bundle at all, so none of this applies there — only
  `tauri build` can be used to check it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>A site you opened in a pane is asking for the camera.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>A site you opened in a pane is asking for the microphone.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
